    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Because the Moon isn't only out at night! It's often up in the day too.",
      "punch": "night",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌙",
        "text": "Not just at night!",
        "cue": "night",
        "sub": "Often up in the day",
        "sub_cue": "often"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "But why?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "The Moon travels around the Earth about once a month. So it rises at a different time each day.",
      "board": {
        "type": "orbit",
        "title": "Moon trip",
        "center": "🌍",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🌙",
            "label": "Moon",
            "cue": "moon"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So sometimes it's up when the Sun is up?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Exactly! On lots of days, the Moon and the Sun are in the sky at the same time.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "☀️",
        "text": "Sun and Moon together",
        "cue": "same",
        "sub": "On lots of days",
        "sub_cue": "lots"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Does the Moon make its own light?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "No! Sunlight shines on the Moon and bounces off it, all the way to our eyes.",
      "punch": "bounces",
      "board": {
        "type": "flow",
        "title": "Moonlight trip",
        "packet": "✨",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "☀️",
            "label": "Sunlight",
            "cue": "sunlight"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🌕",
            "label": "Bounces off",
            "cue": "bounces"
          },
          {
            "icon": "👀",
            "label": "Our eyes",
            "cue": "eyes"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "But the daytime sky is so bright!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "The Moon is bright enough to shine through the blue sky. That's why it looks pale in the day.",
      "board": {
        "type": "picture",
        "art": "moon_day",
        "caption": "Bright enough to see",
        "cue": "bright",
        "icon": "🌕"
